     "opthelp" is a data file displayed during play when you
pick one particular choice for the "?" command.  You shouldn't
mess with it unless you're actually implementing new options.

     I'm not sure what "MacOS X Tiles" actually is; is that
using the Qt interface?  The user options for it can be in
either ".nethackrc" in your home directory or in
"Library/Preferences/Nethack Defaults" (note the space) or
"Library/Preferences/Nethack Defaults.txt".  You'll need to
create one from scratch (as plain text).  Many of the settings
in it will only apply to future new games, not to reloads of
existing saved games.



